   "subject": "Re: xcopy installation of R Open",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">My understanding is that R is extremely portable (<a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/base/rw-FAQ.html#Can-I-run-R-from-a-CD-or-USB-drive_003f\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/base/rw-FAQ.html%23Can-I-run-R-from-a-CD-or-USB-drive_003f&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793241871862000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PlpDwUjcaZln0wDmthFAU\">http://cran.r-project.org/bin/windows/base/rw-FAQ.html#Can-I-run-R-from-a-CD-or-USB-drive_003f</a>) and very few information may be written in the registry during installation (namely version number and association of R with .RData file).<div><br></div><div>Furthermore I experienced no issues in the past by running RRO from a usb portable drive as well.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, 22 May 2015 23:44:07 UTC+2, <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stephen...@revolution-computing.com</a>  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">No, it is not recommended to just copy the installation\r\ndirectory to a different location on Windows systems.</span></p><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Times New Roman\" size=\"3\">\r\n\r\n</font><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">The reason is that R(and Revolution R Open) stores several application-specific\r\nsettings in the Windows registry that would</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">not be copied.</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">Stephen Weller</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0pt\"><br><br>On Thursday, May 21, 2015 at 7:28:26 AM UTC-7, Jiri Pik wrote:</p></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;padding-left:1ex;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-width:1px;border-left-style:solid\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" vlink=\"purple\" link=\"blue\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:11pt\">Hello:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(31,73,125);font-family:&quot;Calibr