   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Jiri,</div><div><br></div><div>A silent install of Revolution R Open can be done the same way it works for CRAN-R:</div><div><br></div><div>1).  Open a DOS window on your system.</div><div>2).  Naivgate to the directory that contains the RR Open installer.</div><div>3).  At the command prompt, type either:</div><div><br></div><div>     RRO-8.0.3-win.exe /SILENT</div><div><br></div><div>     or:</div><div><br></div><div>     </div><div>     RRO-8.0.3-win.exe VERYSILENT</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Hope this helps.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Stephen Weller<br>Data Scientist<br>Microsoft<br></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
